   "harm": "setting validation state to Error in fuzz test causes subsequent validation checks to never run",
   "hash": "a6b14911cf1e6c61",
   "history": [
    {
     "at": "2026-09-18T03:33:51+00:00",
     "blocking": false,
     "by": "run:20260918-0314",
     "cause": "rc:3985017578",
     "status": "resolved"
    }
   ],
   "id": "rc:3985017578",
   "kind": "correctness",
   "other_replies": [],
   "part": 1,
   "pin": null,
   "question": "",
   "quote": "Calling validation_state_pow_and_merkle.Error(\"\") changes the state to Error, making the later if (validation_state_pow_and_merkle.IsValid()) always false so it never runs.",
   "request": "",
   "status": "fixed",
   "status_by": {
    "at": "2026-09-11",
    "by": "optout21",
    "id": "r:5175950623",
    "quote": "Applied fix to a minor fuzz test bug, found in review"
   },
   "status_note": "fixed in push and acknowledged by author",
   "type": "objection",
   "url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/35570#discussion_r3985017578"
  },
  {
   "association": "MEMBER",
   "at": "2026-09-15",
   "author": "hodlinator",
   "author_replies": [
    "rc:4026751594",
    "c:5697346533",
    "rc:4052261603"
   ],
   "clears_with": "change",
   "fix": null,
   "harm": "relying on asserts and comments to enforce that methods never return Error risks unexpected runtime aborts and is fragile compared to type-level enforcement",
   "hash": "a5297e84a606bbdc",
   "history": [
    {
     "at": "2026-09-18T03:33:51+00:00",
     "blocking": true,
     "by": "run:20260918-0314",
     "cause": "rc:4014835740",
     "status": "open"
    }
   ],
   "id": "rc:4014835740",
   "kind": "approach",
   "other_replies": [],
   "part": 1,
   "pin": null,
   "question": "",
   "quote": "It would feel safer if we made the paths which do not return error states instead return a narrower state type which only allowed valid/invalid, instead of having these more imperative checks.",
   "request": "",
   "status": "contested",
   "status_by": null,
   "status_note": "hodlinator prefers type-level enforcement via #35646 before proceeding",
   "type": "objection",
   "url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/35570#discussion_r4014835740"
  }
 ],
